00:00:38.183 --> 00:00:40.523
If you're 30 pounds overweight,
you want to lose 30 pounds,

00:00:40.523 --> 00:00:42.884
do it the right way,
start eating vegetables,

00:00:42.884 --> 00:00:44.553
monitor your calories,
write down what you eat,

00:00:44.553 --> 00:00:48.360
exercise every day,
force yourself to do it.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.821
Say, you're the General.

00:00:49.821 --> 00:00:51.905
The brain is the General,
the troops are the body,

00:00:51.905 --> 00:00:53.671
the troops don't want
to listen but you listen

00:00:53.671 --> 00:00:55.748
and you get up, and you do it.

00:00:55.748 --> 00:00:57.350
And then you get to write it down.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:59.672
And if you don't write it
down, you don't eat, you don't,

00:00:59.672 --> 00:01:02.040
you don't jerk off, you don't shower,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.425
you write that, down so you do it.

00:01:04.425 --> 00:01:05.369
It's like brushing your teeth.

00:01:05.369 --> 00:01:07.285
It's not like, "Eh, I don't
want to brush my teeth today."

00:01:07.285 --> 00:01:08.852
What, do you want your teeth
to rot out of your head

00:01:08.852 --> 00:01:12.650
you, dunce, just do it, just
do it, make yourself do it.

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:15.365
And if you do that, if you
write, down and do that,

00:01:15.365 --> 00:01:17.174
you can change who the, you are.

00:01:17.174 --> 00:01:18.595
- I'm a big believer
in writing things down,

00:01:18.595 --> 00:01:21.688
I have my goals down, my big
goal that I want to accomplish,

00:01:21.688 --> 00:01:24.407
but also my weekly goals
and my daily goals.

00:01:24.407 --> 00:01:26.415
I wake up, I know what I have to do today

00:01:26.415 --> 00:01:29.085
because it's written down
in my Google calendar note.

00:01:29.085 --> 00:01:30.664
And I think this is a key difference

00:01:30.664 --> 00:01:32.921
that can really help
a lot of entrepreneurs

00:01:32.921 --> 00:01:36.574
is understanding planning versus doing.

00:01:36.574 --> 00:01:38.589
I think too many
entrepreneurs are constantly

00:01:38.589 --> 00:01:41.566
in planning mode, and it's
fine to be in planning mode,

00:01:41.566 --> 00:01:43.240
right, you're planning, you're
thinking, you're dreaming,

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:46.093
you're imagining, here's
how I'm going to start

00:01:46.093 --> 00:01:47.499
and then we're going to hire this person,

00:01:47.499 --> 00:01:49.839
then you keep building this
great idea, it just keeps

00:01:49.839 --> 00:01:51.672
getting bigger and bigger and
bigger, and it's exciting.

00:01:51.672 --> 00:01:53.896
You fire off the happiness feelings

00:01:53.896 --> 00:01:56.190
of this great idea that
you're exploding out.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:59.403
But nothing happens until you do, right?

00:01:59.403 --> 00:02:01.993
And sometimes the planning
and the seeing it to the end

00:02:01.993 --> 00:02:04.270
is so exciting, it's so fulfilling,

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:06.214
but then you don't even want to do it

00:02:06.214 --> 00:02:08.202
because you already got the
happiness from doing that,

00:02:08.202 --> 00:02:09.830
and you don't actually
want to do any of the work.

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:12.575
Where most entrepreneurs,
I think, are up here

00:02:12.575 --> 00:02:14.717
with planning and like
down here in execution.

00:02:14.717 --> 00:02:16.670
You got to flip it.

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:18.555
Planning is really important.

00:02:18.555 --> 00:02:20.425
You don't want to just go out and do

00:02:20.425 --> 00:02:21.546
and hope something happens, right?

00:02:21.546 --> 00:02:23.380
That's not the path to having success.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:26.775
So planning is important but
doing is way more important.

00:02:26.775 --> 00:02:29.501
Like, you got to spend way
more time on the execution

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:31.814
versus the planning, and so this is why

00:02:31.814 --> 00:02:33.335
writing things down really helps.

00:02:33.335 --> 00:02:35.416
So when you're in planning
mode, and whether it's

00:02:35.416 --> 00:02:37.256
once a week, or once a
month, or once a quarter,

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:39.966
or some kind of mixture
of whenever you feel like

00:02:39.966 --> 00:02:42.056
your plans aren't going according to plan,

00:02:42.056 --> 00:02:43.365
you create a new plan.

00:02:43.365 --> 00:02:45.373
And say, okay, Monday I'm going to wake up

00:02:45.373 --> 00:02:46.729
and here's what I'm going to work on.

00:02:46.729 --> 00:02:48.316
And when I look at my
Google calendar note,

00:02:48.316 --> 00:02:51.859
and I wake up and I see
Monday and here are my tasks,

00:02:51.859 --> 00:02:54.278
I know what my goal is,
like here's my big goal,

00:02:54.278 --> 00:02:57.438
and then I know how I'm
going to accomplish that,

00:02:57.438 --> 00:02:59.076
and then I know what I need to do today.

00:02:59.076 --> 00:03:02.854
So, the planning mode is
super small on a Monday,

00:03:02.854 --> 00:03:04.543
I'm just reviewing what
I need to get done,

00:03:04.543 --> 00:03:07.795
and then I spend the entire day doing it.

00:03:07.795 --> 00:03:11.108
Executing, making tons of progress.

00:03:11.108 --> 00:03:13.499
How am I able to make three videos a day

00:03:13.499 --> 00:03:15.111
for my YouTube channel?

00:03:15.111 --> 00:03:17.280
Yes I have a team, yes
they help me tremendously,

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.095
and yes we have a plan in place, right,

00:03:21.095 --> 00:03:22.911
of how to structure the
day and how to film,

00:03:22.911 --> 00:03:24.899
and what goes up and content review,

00:03:24.899 --> 00:03:26.566
and a whole system and architecture,

00:03:26.566 --> 00:03:28.482
and we constantly work
to improve that plan,

00:03:28.482 --> 00:03:32.233
but it's, most of the time
we're spending time doing.

00:03:32.233 --> 00:03:35.318
Like, I am executing, Christine
and my editor is executing,

00:03:35.318 --> 00:03:38.316
the people on my team are
executing, we're doing the work.

00:03:38.316 --> 00:03:41.314
And so, you need to get
out of the planning mode

00:03:41.314 --> 00:03:44.654
and more into the execution mode.

00:03:44.654 --> 00:03:46.658
And if you don't write things down,

00:03:46.658 --> 00:03:51.531
then you stay in planning mode
too much, at least I find.

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:54.026
If I woke up and I didn't know
what I was going to do today

00:03:54.026 --> 00:03:56.257
and I didn't have a plan, then
I'd wake up and make a plan.

00:03:56.257 --> 00:03:57.517
Right?

00:03:57.517 --> 00:03:59.770
I'd make a plan, and then
start from the top again,

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:02.249
and then, I would spend a
good chunk of time planning

00:04:02.249 --> 00:04:05.474
and not enough time actually doing.

00:04:05.474 --> 00:04:06.875
And if I did that every day I'd be losing

00:04:06.875 --> 00:04:09.541
so much time to planning
that I would never

00:04:09.541 --> 00:04:11.536
get as much done as I could get done.

00:04:11.536 --> 00:04:13.913
So planning is important, and you need

00:04:13.913 --> 00:04:15.752
to spend time planning and you figure out,

00:04:15.752 --> 00:04:18.349
what is your execution game plan, right?

00:04:18.349 --> 00:04:19.182
Good.

00:04:19.182 --> 00:04:22.140
And then most of your
time, 90% of your time

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:24.242
is spent actually doing the work.

00:04:24.242 --> 00:04:25.916
And then you come back at some point like,

00:04:25.916 --> 00:04:29.091
did this work work,
did it lead to results,

00:04:29.091 --> 00:04:30.842
is this the best use of my time?

00:04:30.842 --> 00:04:32.596
You can come back to planning
mode every now and then,

00:04:32.596 --> 00:04:35.162
and make some adjustments
then go out and test it again,

00:04:35.162 --> 00:04:37.581
but this is where you need
to spend most of your time.

00:04:37.581 --> 00:04:41.349
The work, the doing, the
execution, the hard stuff.

00:04:41.349 --> 00:04:45.266
Versus the planning, the
thinking, the dreaming only.

00:04:45.266 --> 00:04:47.511
You need both pieces, but
you got to play more here

00:04:47.511 --> 00:04:49.576
than over here.

